    "body": "<!-- pr-reviewer: 8d63209a72490a4fffe6b36f4e2cc6c3d6adde1a -->\n**Review @ 8d63209a: clean**, `merge-ready`.\n\n- The fix is one new arm in `descent::plan_arm`, `Entry3D::Ramp if m.ring_zig`. Only the circular kernel sets `ring_zig`, so pocket, contour and bore do not change. The arm uses `ramp_fallback`, the zig-zag of the helix along the ring at the ramp angle. If the ring is too short for that angle, the tool dives at the plunge feed, and the path names the dive.\n- Mutation, run here: with the arm disabled (`false && m.ring_zig`), both pins in `circular_ramp_angle` fail. With the arm restored, they pass 2/2.\n- These neighbour suites also pass: `circular_arcs` 5/5 and `level_links` 12/12.\n- No golden moved, because no golden has a Circular with a Ramp entry. The posted G-code changes only for that case, and the `Changelog:` line says so.\n- The PR does not touch `ring.rs`.\n\nNot blocking: the author asks if a pocket ring or a bore with a Ramp entry and no stated angle gets the same zero-length chord. Nobody probed this. Please file a follow-up issue if a probe shows it.\n",
    "author_association": "COLLABORATOR",
